# EDJE Compass — application read surface (ADR-008)
#
# NOT the published Directory boundary. These routes carry no /v1 prefix because they are the Compass
# SPA's own surface: session-authenticated, projected per viewer tier, and versioned with the SPA
# rather than as a stable contract for out-of-monolith consumers.
#
# Authentication only — no Compass role required (AC-5, AC-12, FR-001). What a baseline viewer sees is
# scoped per FIELD by the projection, not all-or-nothing by the gate.
#
# Locally, X-Dev-Roles overrides the DevBypass identity's roles. DevBypass carries the nine timesheet
# roles, which resolve to tier Baseline in Compass — Compass inherits nothing.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5009

### Team Directory — default view (active EDJErs, hire-date order)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/team-directory

### Search by partial last name (case-insensitive)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/team-directory?search=smi

### Filter by employee type
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/team-directory?employeeType=Full Time

### Filter by state
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/team-directory?state=OH

### Filter to one coach's team, by the coach's own id (issue #655)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/team-directory?coachId=9

### Both filters together (conjunctive)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/team-directory?employeeType=Full Time&state=OH

### Sort by a column, descending
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/team-directory?sort=lastName&desc=true

### As an elevated role — inactive EDJErs become reachable
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/team-directory?status=all
X-Dev-Roles: Compass Admin

### As an elevated role — inactive only
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/team-directory?status=inactive
X-Dev-Roles: Compass Admin

### As a baseline viewer, forging the filter — MUST still return no inactive EDJEr (FR-011a)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/team-directory?status=all

### Empty result is a 200 with an empty list, never a 404 (FR-013)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/team-directory?search=zzzznobody

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sales Dashboard and reports (feature 007) — RolePolicy.CompassReporting: Compass Sales, Compass Ops
# or Compass Super Admin. A Compass Admin holding no other Compass role gets 403 on every request
# below, by design (FR-019) — the refusal is server-side, not a hidden nav link.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Sales Dashboard — the four tile counts plus the as-of business date (AC-36)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/dashboard

### Tile drill-down — one route, four categories (AC-37)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/dashboard/breakdown/expiring-sows

### The other three categories
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/dashboard/breakdown/active-sows

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/dashboard/breakdown/confirmed-rollouts

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/dashboard/breakdown/beach

### An unrecognised category is 404, never a silent fallback to one of the four
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/dashboard/breakdown/not-a-category

### Availability Report — three sections: currently available, confirmed rollouts, unconfirmed SOWs (AC-38)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/reports/availability

### Client Assignment Duration — one row per EDJEr-client PAIR, longest tenure first (AC-39)
# Excludes any pair whose only active assignment is at an internal ("beach") client (issue #335).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/reports/assignment-duration

### Assignment Start lookup — every assignment starting in the INCLUSIVE range (AC-40)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/reports/assignment-start?from=2024-01-01&to=2026-12-31

### from > to is a 400 with a message, never a silent swap and never an empty list
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/reports/assignment-start?from=2026-12-31&to=2024-01-01

### SOW Extension Report — every extension SOW starting in the INCLUSIVE range (issue #534)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/reports/sow-extension?from=2024-01-01&to=2026-12-31

### from > to is a 400 with a message, never a silent swap and never an empty list
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/reports/sow-extension?from=2026-12-31&to=2024-01-01

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CSV export (issue #337). Same group, so the SAME RolePolicy.CompassReporting applies — an export
# hands over the whole population in one request, so it must not be a more permissive second door.
#
# AC-NFR-6 still forbids PDF and print; the CSV ban was spec 007's own inference and was withdrawn
# (spec Deviation 12). Every CSV carries a UTF-8 BOM so Excel decodes non-ASCII names.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Availability Report — ALL THREE sections, zipped
# A zip rather than one CSV because the three sections do not share a column set: merging them would
# have to drop columns or invent them.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/reports/availability/export

### One section at a time: currently-available | confirmed-rollouts | unconfirmed-sows
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/reports/availability/export?section=currently-available

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/reports/availability/export?section=confirmed-rollouts

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/reports/availability/export?section=unconfirmed-sows

### An unrecognised section is a 400, never an empty file
# An empty CSV is indistinguishable from "that section has no rows" — a different and wrong answer.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/reports/availability/export?section=not-a-section

### Client Assignment Duration as CSV
# Carries `Total Days` alongside the display string: "3 yrs 4 mos (1,238 days)" sorts lexically in a
# spreadsheet, which puts "10 yrs" before "3 yrs".
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/reports/assignment-duration/export

### Assignment Start lookup as CSV, for the same inclusive range
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/reports/assignment-start/export?from=2024-01-01&to=2026-12-31

### The export repeats the screen's inverted-range guard rather than answering an empty file
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/reports/assignment-start/export?from=2026-12-31&to=2024-01-01

### SOW Extension Report as CSV, for the same inclusive range (issue #534)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/reports/sow-extension/export?from=2024-01-01&to=2026-12-31

### The export repeats the screen's inverted-range guard rather than answering an empty file
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/reports/sow-extension/export?from=2026-12-31&to=2024-01-01
